  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "placementWhy": "Moderate (about 20-30 m): free similarity fit on three cenotes, residuals 5 m (Nariz), 19 m (Aktun-Hu) and 14 m (Cueva Seca); 1.210 m/px, 0.7 degrees. The map has no scale bar and no north arrow (north taken as up, as the fit confirms). Nariz is the trusted point (Open Caves source, located on site); Aktun-Hu (Gerrard 2015) and Cueva Seca (map source) are not, so the scale and rotation were checked independently: (1) the map's own penetrations (p.1800 at Nariz to p.3600 at El Cruzero, p.3600 to p.6500/p.5200/p.7650, p.800 to p.1800) measured along the drawn lines give 1.15-1.25 m/px; (2) a free fit of these lines onto the Aktun-Hu lines of the placed QRSS 2012 overview (sac-actun-mpo-tulum, placed independently of these cenotes) gives 1.226 m/px and 0.5 degrees; after this placement the two line sets are a median 20 m apart (the overview is drawn at 9.5 m/px), with no systematic shift (about 10 m). Cabeza Azteca (Gerrard 2015) is a check point: the map's dot lands 95 m NW of it, and a fit including it would need 1.32 m/px, which the penetrations and the overview both reject - the database position is probably off. Canopy everywhere: no cenote pond shows on the Mapbox/Maxar imagery, and OSM has no water or cave feature on the map's area. The Google Earth line plots (sac-aktun-*-google) carry no Aktun-Hu lines, only placemarks equal to the database positions (not independent). Tunel NE's end (p.4792) stops about 550 m SW of the placed Hoyo Negro (hoyo-negro-2012): no overlap, as expected (Hoyo Negro is reached from Ich Balam / Outland, not drawn here).",
