    "why": "b/w stick map (guidelines only, no walls), traced as lines. Cenotes are blue dots on the lines (ink too: their skeleton is a short line through the dot). Every label, depth and penetration is boxed out (survey-lines tracing doesn't skip symbol ink) and listed by hand under symbols. joinShortPx/snapEndsPx: at junctions the skeleton left 1-7 px gaps where the ink is continuous (checked one by one); they are closed. The short line under the Cenote Aktun-Hu dot starts 2 px below the dot without touching it: kept as drawn."
